# Commit & PR Rules (Shared Atom)

> Applies to: Frontend-Developer, Backend-Developer, QA-Tester

---

## 1. Commit Convention

### Subject = Branch Name (MANDATORY)
```bash
git commit -m "$(git branch --show-current)" -m "<body>"
```

### Body Format
```
<issue_title_from_github>

<first_2-3_lines_of_issue>

<code_changes_summary>

Refs #<issue_number>
```

---

## 2. Pre-Commit Checklist

- [ ] Remove all `console.*` calls
- [ ] No hard-coded values (use env/constants)
- [ ] No dead code or unused variables
- [ ] TypeScript: no errors
- [ ] ESLint: clean
- [ ] Build: success

---

## 3. Pull Request Rules

### 3.1 Use `--body-file` (MANDATORY)
```bash
# ✅ CORRECT
node scripts/generate-pr-body.js  # → scripts/pr-body.md
gh pr create --body-file scripts/pr-body.md --base test

# ❌ WRONG — truncates on Windows
gh pr create --body "## Summary\n..."
```

### 3.2 PR Body — Only 3 Sections
```markdown
## Summary
**Branch:** `<branch>`
**Feature:** #<number> - <title>
<1-2 sentence description>

## Changelog
| Version | Date | Time | Author | Description |
|---------|------|------|--------|-------------|

## Testing
- Production build passed
- No TypeScript errors
- No linting errors
- No console logs
- QA report sent to Telegram

Closes #<number>
```

### 3.3 Target Branch Rule

| Source Branch | Base Branch |
|--------------|-------------|
| `feature/*` | `test` |
| `bugfix/*` | `test` |
| `hotfix/*` | `main` |
| `release/*` | `main` |

### 3.4 Auto-Assign (MANDATORY)
```bash
PR_NUMBER=$(gh pr view --json number -q .number)
gh pr edit $PR_NUMBER --add-assignee PersonalProjectJob
```

### 3.5 PR Title
```
<branch_name>: <short_summary>
```

---

## 4. Quick Commands

```bash
# Get current branch
git branch --show-current

# Parse issue number (bash)
echo "$BRANCH" | grep -oP '^\w+/(\d+)' | grep -oP '\d+$'

# Determine base branch
if [[ "$BRANCH" == hotfix/* ]]; then BASE="main"; else BASE="test"; fi

# Create PR
gh pr create --head $BRANCH --base $BASE --body-file scripts/pr-body.md

# Assign
gh pr edit $(gh pr view --json number -q .number) --add-assignee PersonalProjectJob
```
